<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS5" title="In 4. Four families from finite geometries ‣ Chow and chain polynomials of matroids are not log-concave" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.5 </span>Three-connected rank-<math class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math> counterexamples</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S5" title="In Chow and chain polynomials of matroids are not log-concave" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-polynomials of graph associahedra are not log-concave</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS1" title="In 5. ℎ-polynomials of graph associahedra are not log-concave ‣ Chow and chain polynomials of matroids are not log-concave" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.1 </span>The graphs</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS2" title="In 5. ℎ-polynomials of graph associahedra are not log-concave ‣ Chow and chain polynomials of matroids are not log-concave" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.2 </span>Computing multichain counts by a transfer matrix</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS3" title="In 5. ℎ-polynomials of graph associahedra are not log-concave ‣ Chow and chain polynomials of matroids are not log-concave" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.3 </span>Why the two parts compete</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS4" title="In 5. ℎ-polynomials of graph associahedra are not log-concave ‣ Chow and chain polynomials of matroids are not log-concave" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.4 </span>A counterexample</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
