<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line ltx_leqno">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Chow and chain polynomials 
<br class="ltx_break">of matroids are not log-concave</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Gergely Bérczi
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_address"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Address: </span>G. Bérczi, Department of Mathematics,
Aarhus University
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email address: </span><a href="mailto:gergely.berczi@math.au.dk">gergely.berczi@math.au.dk</a>
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">, </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Basile Coron
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_address"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Address: </span>B. Coron, LAREMA, Angers, France
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email address: </span><a href="mailto:basile.coron@univ-angers.fr">basile.coron@univ-angers.fr</a>
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">, </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Christopher Eur
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_address"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Address: </span>C. Eur, Carnegie Mellon University, Pittsburgh, PA. USA.
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email address: </span><a href="mailto:ceur@cmu.edu">ceur@cmu.edu</a>
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before"> and </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Shiyue Li
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_address"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Address: </span>S. Li, Department of Mathematics, University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, USA
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email address: </span><a href="mailto:shiyueli@umich.edu">shiyueli@umich.edu</a>
</span></span></span></span></div>
<div class="ltx_dates">Date: October 12, 2026</div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract.</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">The Hilbert–Poincaré series of the Chow rings of the toric varieties of matroids, often called the <em id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Chow polynomials</em>, and the <math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-polynomial of their boundary complexes, called the <em id="abstract1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">chain polynomials</em>, have been conjectured to only have real zeros. We construct several explicit infinite families of matroids from finite geometries, whose multichain counts fail to be log-concave. They share a common geometric construction called <em id="abstract1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hyperplane coalescence</em>, together with several classical operations in projective geometry and combinatorial designs. This induces failures of log-concavity for Chow, augmented Chow, chain, and <math id="abstract1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-polynomials of several explicit infinite families of matroids, disproving the real-rootedness conjectures of Ferroni–Schröter, Huh–Stevens, and Athanasiadis–Kalampogia-Evangelinou from the lowest possible ranks.</p>
    
<p id="abstract1.2" class="ltx_p">As an application of the same mechanism, we also give counterexamples to the log-concavity of <math id="abstract1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-polynomials of graph associahedra, answering in the negative a question of Sack.</p>
  
</div>
<nav class="ltx_TOC ltx_list_toc ltx_toc_toc"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_contents">Contents</h6>
<ol class="ltx_toclist">
